1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
A documentary assistant editor logs a hundred hours of footage by hand: who, where, what time of day, what size.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,000
It takes weeks. Then the editor asks for a rainy night close-up of two people...

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
...and half a day disappears into the log sheet. Shot Memory makes the log write itself.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:28,500
Four public-domain films, 2,166 shots. Gemini watched every one and wrote the log: caption, people, time of day, shot size, tension.

5
00:00:29,266 --> 00:00:32,732
Ask in plain language. The Librarian agent embeds the request...

6
00:00:32,732 --> 00:00:38,332
...writes one hybrid SQL query, and runs it through the official ClickHouse MCP server. Hard filters and vector distance in the same statement.

7
00:00:38,332 --> 00:00:44,332
ClickHouse answers in tens of milliseconds. The SQL panel shows exactly what the agent ran.

8
00:00:44,332 --> 00:00:50,332
Hover a card to play the shot. Every card carries the metadata Gemini extracted.

9
00:00:50,332 --> 00:00:54,832
Similar runs a vector neighbour search on the shot's own embedding.

10
00:00:54,832 --> 00:00:57,832
Now an editing brief.

11
00:01:01,299 --> 00:01:05,299
The CutAssembler splits the brief into beats and sends the Librarian out for each one, in parallel.

12
00:01:05,332 --> 00:01:14,332
Every tool call from every agent streams to the panel: embed_query, run_query, check_metadata, compare_frames.

13
00:01:14,332 --> 00:01:18,566
The ContinuityChecker applies time-of-day and interior/exterior rules from ClickHouse metadata, then asks Gemini to look at the frames.

14
00:01:18,566 --> 00:01:24,566
The timeline lands with the sequence, its total length, and continuity warnings the editor can act on.

15
00:01:24,566 --> 00:01:29,566
Reorder, drop a shot...

16
00:01:29,566 --> 00:01:33,066
...and export a CMX3600 EDL for Resolve, Premiere, or Final Cut.

17
00:01:33,299 --> 00:01:41,299
Under the hood: Google ADK runs the agent team, and Gemini 3.8 Flash makes every model call.

18
00:01:41,299 --> 00:01:49,299
ClickHouse is not a chatbot backend. It is the agents' long-term memory, joined at runtime through mcp-clickhouse.

19
00:01:49,299 --> 00:01:57,232
Remove ClickHouse and nothing works: search, assembly, and continuity checks all read from one table.

20
00:01:57,232 --> 00:02:09,199
Shot Memory. Search hundreds of thousands of shots in plain language, and let the agents assemble the first cut.
